             - { name: SANDBOX_HOST_NFS_ROOT, value: "/mnt/workspaces" }
+            # #775: ceiling for the per-ITEM uv download caches, together.
+            # Unset = no ceiling and nothing is evicted. They outlive their
+            # sandboxes on purpose (a cold start re-uses what that item already
+            # fetched) and live on the pod's OWN disk, which has no declared
+            # ephemeral-storage limit — so leaving this unset trades a slow cold
+            # start for a pod the kubelet may evict. Swept on the idle tick,
+            # least-recently-used first, never one a live sandbox may write to.
+            # ⚠️ The sweep rides the idle reaper, so `SANDBOX_HOST_IDLE_TTL: 0`
+            # (documented as 'reaper off') switches this off with it — and the
+            # tool-cache ceiling too. The host now says so on startup naming the
+            # ceilings it is dropping, because a comment here is not where
+            # anyone looks when the disk fills up.
